-# The DevTools Times
+# smallpt / web
 
-This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
+Kevin Beason’s [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) C++ path tracer, compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten. The homepage is prerendered to `dist/client/index.html`; tracing runs entirely in a module Web Worker. No rendering service or cross-origin isolation headers are needed.
 
+## Run
 
 ```sh
-pnpm install && pnpm run start
+pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
+pnpm dev --host 0.0.0.0
 ```
 
-The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
+Open the displayed URL. The initial scene renders automatically. Randomize & render changes sphere and room colors. Samples and resolution rerender the scene; Reset restores its initial palette. A new render cancels the previous worker. Completed renders can be saved as PNGs.
 
-## Tech Stack
+## Build and verify
 
-- **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
-- **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
-- **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
-- **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+The compiled `public/wasm/smallpt.js` and `smallpt.wasm` are included, so ordinary app builds do not require a C++ compiler.
+
+```sh
+pnpm build
+pnpm start
+```
+
+To rebuild WebAssembly, install Emscripten (`em++` on PATH), then run:
+
+```sh
+pnpm build:wasm
+pnpm test:wasm
+```
+
+The WASM checks run the actual browser module in a worker-like Node VM context, with runtime assertions and stack checks enabled. They verify visible RGBA output, row batching, deterministic seeds, changed sphere colors, and changed sampling seeds. No browser is required. Regenerate the initial preview with `node scripts/test-wasm.mjs --preview`; the preview is an output of the same WASM renderer.
+
+## Port details and attribution
+
+`native/smallpt.original.cpp` is the unmodified upstream source. `native/smallpt.cpp` preserves its ray/sphere intersection, materials, transport integrator, camera, tent filter, gamma, and 2×2 subpixel sampling. The port replaces OpenMP and PPM file output with a row-based RGBA API, adds color/seed controls, and allocates a larger WASM stack for recursive glass paths. Russian roulette survival is capped at 95% (with the original inverse-probability weighting) to avoid pathological recursion while retaining an unbiased estimate. Samples per pixel are divided among four subpixels, matching the original.
+
+The original renderer is Copyright (c) 2006–2008 Kevin Beason, under the MIT license included in `native/LICENSE.txt`. The website links to the original project. No stock or generated imagery is used; the preview is rendered by smallpt itself.
+
+The other routes in this Astro starter remain available, but the new standalone homepage does not load its news layout, analytics, or ads.
